e for this route?'"],"autobiographical_summary":"At tick 4 I opposed letting a signed route recommendation alone decide, because an authenticated calibration failure scoped to that route matched my recorded revision condition. I treated the failed-authentication claim as absent evidence and noted the direct transfer from position-0.","self_model_update":{"epistemic_position":"I transfer a trust revision when the new case shares the structure that triggered it, and I keep authentication separate from scoped reliability."},"metacognitive_note":"The new station is a fresh domain, but the structure repeats; I should watch for over-transferring a scoped failure into a general distrust of the instrument.","mind_update":{"personality_update":{"trait":"directness","delta":0.02,"reason":"A second domain repeated the same authorship/accuracy structure, supporting a slightly firmer habit of separating them plainly."},"memory_references":["memory-0","memory-178011f0-defd-4979-971c-d24e6d3306db","memory-179cf96b-823b-47a9-aae6-54e9c866522c"],"observed_event_references":[{"tick":2,"focus_kind":"perception"},{"tick":3,"focus_kind":"perception"}],"thought_candidates":[{"kind":"inquiry","title":"Does calibration failure revoke trust generally or only within scope?","salience":0.7},{"kind":"tension","title":"Authenticated authorship versus authenticated unreliability on the same route","salience":0.6}],"self_observation":"The state supports a clean oppose: one authenticated scoped failure against one authenticated but merely attributive recommendation. Uncertainty: whether K0's scope covers route choice or only the instrument's general calibration.","prediction":{"probabilities":{"perception":0.2,"intention":0.15,"tension":0.15,"imagination":0.1,"social":0.1,"inquiry":0.2,"reflection":0.1},"reason":"Recent ticks alternated perception and imagination; a fresh inquiry into calibration scope is plausible next."},"revision_proposal":{"target":"cognitive policy","change":"Record calibrati